---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Keep this current. Update the date and the lines below when things change.
const updated = "June 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Now — Debanjan"
  description="What Debanjan is focused on right now — work, writing, and what he's learning."
>
  <div class="eyebrow">Now · updated {updated}</div>
  <hr class="rule" />
  <h1>Now</h1>
  <p class="lede">A snapshot of what has my attention. Inspired by the <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">/now page</a> idea.</p>

  <h2>Working on</h2>
  <p>Email deliverability and sequences at Apollo.io — inbox placement, sequence correctness, and the pipeline paths that have to stay right under retries, overload, and partial failure.</p>

  <h2>Writing</h2>
  <p>Publishing short production notes: message accounting, retry storms, and related failure modes. Prefer one concrete incident over a generic reliability essay.</p>

  <h2>Thinking about</h2>
  <p>Incident calm without heroics, better questions in design review, and protecting focus over the long run. Sustained attention is a finite resource; how you spend it is an engineering decision too.</p>

  <h2>Learning</h2>
  <p>Small tools when a problem is genuinely mine to solve. Building beats passive consumption.</p>

  <p class="linkline" style="margin-top:40px">
    <a href="/about">about →</a> ·
    <a href="/writing">writing →</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
